Z||000003||StuGood||08-20-2001||01:28 AM||||Delano (west side) - but I doubt you've seen me, since lately I'm "Fiero-poor   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">"  The only one I drive now is a 1988 coupe, which needs <B>much</B> work to get it into shape.<P>My current project, though, is a 1987 GT which ran fine until I started tearing it down to fix valve seals and exhaust manifold bolts - and the further I got, the more I wanted to clean/ fix/ paint, etc.  Ain't that the way it always is   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">?  Give me a while get it on the road again.    <P>After that, Stu learns how to do the clutch in his 1986 gold SE V6 4-speed!<P>So, in a few weeks from now, if you're tooling down McLean Boulevard in your Fiero, and a silver Fiero GT coming at you lifts its left headlight and "winks" (flashes) at you, you'll know it's me! <P>BTW, is there a good, reasonable, auto upholsterer in town that you can recommend?  Someone mentioned Morgan Bulley to me earlier.  Remember, "Beats me -I don't know" is an acceptable answer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 08-20-2001).]||||reg||7
